counts that the European Central Bank and Eurostat publish for the euro area and its countries, at market value, in euros. Non-residents are holders outside the euro area. These are the debt securities of banks, money market funds, investment funds, insurers, pension funds and other financial firms, short and long term together, at market value; covered bonds and securitisations are inside. Company bonds have their own book. Net bought is the quarterly transactions; price and other changes is the change in holdings minus what was bought. The split by kind of holder starts in December 2013; before that only the total is published, and the full table keeps it. Source: European Central Bank and Eurostat, Quarterly Sector Accounts. Shares of the total, remainders and groupings are our calculations, and the ECB and Eurostat are not responsible for them."}